From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Read the aperture size option once per boot

With mrc.bin haswell_igd_set_aperture() runs before and after raminit,
and read the option from the store in flash both times. Keep the value
in a static: both runs are in romstage.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c | 17 +++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
index 779ff23c51..d3625f12a0 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
@@ -104,12 +104,17 @@ static unsigned int igd_aperture_mib(enum igd_aperture_size size)
 void haswell_igd_set_aperture(void)
 {
 	const pci_devfn_t igd = PCI_DEV(0, 2, 0);
-	unsigned int size = get_uint_option("gfx_aperture_size", IGD_APERTURE_256MB);
-
-	if (size != IGD_APERTURE_128MB && size != IGD_APERTURE_256MB &&
-	    size != IGD_APERTURE_512MB) {
-		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "IGD: invalid gfx_aperture_size %u, using 256 MiB\n", size);
-		size = IGD_APERTURE_256MB;
+	/* Read once: the option store is in flash, and MRC calls for a second run */
+	static unsigned int size = ~0U;
+
+	if (size == ~0U) {
+		size = get_uint_option("gfx_aperture_size", IGD_APERTURE_256MB);
+		if (size != IGD_APERTURE_128MB && size != IGD_APERTURE_256MB &&
+		    size != IGD_APERTURE_512MB) {
+			printk(BIOS_WARNING, "IGD: invalid gfx_aperture_size %u, using 256 MiB\n",
+			       size);
+			size = IGD_APERTURE_256MB;
+		}
 	}
 
 	const u8 old = pci_read_config8(igd, MSAC);
-- 
